{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1784646302,"nonce":"4Hr4Nyd1vWZaKAkhX0ThJVWp7q4=","message":"Root-cause analysis (no fix proposed).\n\nThe \"partial\" status is derived from **persistent tracking metadata, not the\nbranch's actual contents**, and the upgrade handler refuses \"partial\".\n\nTaking one patch writes a `taken` marker on that patch and recomputes\n`status='partial'` (any patch missing `taken` =\u003e partial) in\n`_record_take_metadata` (`src/b4/review_tui/_tracking_app.py:2655-2661`),\npersisted in the tracking commit's JSON. Reverting the cherry-pick on the\n*target* branch does not touch the tracking commit, so the `taken` marker and\n`partial` status survive and are re-read on rescan. Nothing clears a `taken`\nmarker from branch state.\n\nThe upgrade action then refuses: `action_update_revision`\n(`_tracking_app.py:3781`) permits only `reviewing`/`new`, otherwise notifies\n\"Series must be checked out or new to upgrade\".\n\nCompounding UX inconsistency: the action menu *offers* upgrade for partial\nseries (`_tracking_app.py:1358-1361`:\n`if status in ('reviewing','partial') and ...has_newer`), but the handler\nrejects it -- so the option is shown and then fails. Applying then reverting\nthe remaining patches flips the status out of \"partial\" into a permitted state,\nwhich is the reporter's \"unstick\" workaround.\n\nSame upgrade-gating family as 08646dc (b4 review series version upgrade flow\nawkwardness).","files":null}]}